# Code Review Rule

## ⚠️ CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS

### 1. Validation Requirement
**Before flagging ANY issue, you MUST validate it against the "Legitimate Patterns & Exceptions" section and complete the mandatory validation checklist. Context and intent matter more than rigid rule application.**

### 2. Format Selection (MANDATORY)
**DEFAULT**: Use **TERSE FORMAT** for all standard review commands
**EXPLICIT REQUEST ONLY**: Use **VERBOSE FORMAT** when user specifically requests detailed/comprehensive/verbose analysis

**Terse Format Triggers** (Use terse format):
- "Review my changes"
- "Run code review" 
- "Code review [component]"
- "Review [component-name]"
- Any standard review request

**Verbose Format Triggers** (Use verbose format):
- "Run **detailed** code review"
- "Perform **verbose** review"
- "Run **comprehensive** code review"
- "**Detailed** review of [component]"
- Explicit mention of "detailed", "verbose", "comprehensive", or "in-depth"

## Overview
Performs comprehensive, **context-aware** code review of git changes or entire codebase using project-specific rules and industry best practices. Reviews are based on the established Spectrum component guidelines and output structured feedback for resolution. **Emphasizes pattern recognition and validation over rigid rule enforcement.**

**Output Format**: Terse (concise, actionable) by default. Verbose (comprehensive analysis) only on explicit request.

